# cvvdp-fork Phase 8b — diffmap distribution capture
# Date: 2026-05-25
# Encoder commit: cvvdp-fork-rfc + diffmap dump scaffolding (af80bfad)
# Harness: jxl-encoder/examples/cvvdp_phase8b_diffmap_distribution.rs
# Hook: maybe_dump_diffmap_stats() in jxl-encoder/src/vardct/perceptual_backend.rs
#
# Run:
#   JXL_CVVDP_DIFFMAP_RENORM_SCALE=1.0 \
#     ./target/release/examples/cvvdp_phase8b_diffmap_distribution \
#     --dump-out /tmp/cvvdp_p8b_dump.tsv \
#     --out benchmarks/cvvdp_diffmap_distribution_2026-05-25.tsv
#
# Fixtures (5 cells × 4 distances = 20 (image, distance) pairs):
#   CID22/1025469.png  (photo, mid-mass)
#   CID22/1418519.png  (photo, low-detail)
#   CID22/1189261.png  (photo, high-detail)
#   GB82-SC/terminal.png  (screenshot, text-heavy)
#   GB82-SC/imac_g3.png   (screenshot, UI-heavy)
# Distances: 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0
# Effort: 8 (buttloop fires at e≥8)
# Buttloop iters: 3 per encode (libjxl default at e=8 = 2 + 1 compare-only)
#
# Column schema (cvvdp_diffmap_distribution_2026-05-25.tsv):
#   cell                  — "corpus/image|d=N" key
#   n_iters_b             — number of B_CPU diffmap dumps captured (== buttloop iters)
#   n_iters_c             — number of C_GPU_PRE / C_CPU_PRE diffmap dumps
#   mean_b                — mean of per-iter butter diffmap means
#   mean_c                — mean of per-iter cvvdp diffmap means (PRE-renorm)
#   ratio_c_over_b        — mean_c / mean_b (single per-cell scalar)
#
# Headline aggregates (computed by the harness):
#   n cells: 20
#   median cvvdp/butter mean ratio: 1.5147
#   p25..p75 range:                 [0.7048, 2.5220]
#   global cvvdp/butter mean ratio: 2.1757
#   geometric mean ratio:           1.3334
#
# **CORRECTION (2026-05-25 post-bench)**: The mean-ratio alone is NOT the
# right scale. The buttloop's bad-block predicate fires on
# `tile_dist / effective_metric_target > 1`, and `effective_metric_target`
# differs between backends (butter: distance=2.0; cvvdp: 0.0724 at d=2).
# The RIGHT scale satisfies:
#   `(mean_c * scale) / target_c ≈ mean_b / target_b`
#   → scale = (target_c / target_b) * (mean_b / mean_c)
#
# Per-cell target-aware scale (from this same Phase 8b data):
#   median:  0.0177    geomean:  0.0163    mean: 0.0213
#   p25:     0.0103    p75:      0.0234
#   min:     0.0036 (terminal d=0.5)    max: 0.0707 (imac_g3 d=1.0)
#
# Per-distance medians:
#   d=0.5: 0.0164    d=1.0: 0.0306
#   d=2.0: 0.0224    d=3.0: 0.0178
#
# **===> SHIPPED Phase 8c CVVDP_DIFFMAP_RENORM_SCALE = 0.018**
# (rounded median of target-aware per-cell scales; the placeholder 0.660
# derived from mean-only ratio was wrong-direction by ~37× and verified
# to make bytes WORSE in the Phase 8c first re-bench attempt).
#
# Per-(image, distance) ratio table (sorted by distance for readability):
#
#   image                        | d=0.5  | d=1.0  | d=2.0  | d=3.0
#   ----------------------------------------------------------------
#   CID22/1025469.png            | 0.57   | 1.20   | 2.52   | 3.94
#   CID22/1189261.png            | 0.33   | 0.75   | 1.51   | 2.49
#   CID22/1418519.png            | 0.34   | 0.78   | 1.62   | 2.50
#   GB82-SC/imac_g3.png          | 0.35   | 0.34   | 0.70   | 1.42
#   GB82-SC/terminal.png         | 1.61   | 6.52   | 7.84   | 4.83
#
# Patterns:
#
#   1. Photos: ratio MONOTONICALLY GROWS with distance. At d=0.5 cvvdp
#      diffmap mean is ~1/3 of butter's (cvvdp is tame on subtle perturbations);
#      at d=3.0 it's 2.5-3.9× larger (cvvdp's pyramid + CSF amplifies obvious
#      artifacts more than butteraugli's max-norm).
#
#   2. Screenshots split:
#      - imac_g3.png follows photo pattern (0.35 → 1.42), but lower magnitude.
#      - terminal.png is anomalous: cvvdp 1.6-7.8× larger at every distance.
#        Likely because terminal's high-contrast text edges trip cvvdp's CSF
#        much harder than butter's max-norm averaging.
#
#   3. Single global scale CANNOT satisfy every cell. Median 1.5147 picks
#      the central tendency; that's our Phase 8c production constant.
#      Outliers (terminal, high-d photos) will remain slightly over-allocated
#      under Phase 8c; Phase 8d bytes-tighten exit is the next lever.
#
# Decision rationale:
#
# We pick the MEDIAN cvvdp/butter ratio (1.5147) for the renorm scale because:
#   (a) Median is robust to the per-(image, distance) outliers in the
#       distribution (1.6-7.8× on terminal).
#   (b) Half of cells will be slightly over-scaled, half slightly under-scaled
#       — symmetric error tolerance.
#   (c) Geometric mean (1.33) and median (1.51) agree within 14% — the central
#       tendency is well-defined.
#   (d) Global ratio (2.18) is pulled by the screenshot outliers; using it
#       would over-scale most cells.
#
# What the renorm DOES to the per-block reducer:
#
#   Pre-renorm: tile_dist = K_TILE_NORM * (mean(cvvdp_diff^16))^(1/16)
#               diff = tile_dist / effective_metric_target_distance
#               bad-block if diff > 1.0
#   Post-renorm (scale s=0.660): cvvdp_diff *= 0.660
#                tile_dist_new = K_TILE_NORM * (mean((0.660 * cvvdp_diff)^16))^(1/16)
#                             = 0.660 * tile_dist
#   so the new diff = 0.660 * tile_dist / effective_metric_target_distance
#   The bad-block threshold of 1.0 is unchanged; but cvvdp values that
#   exceeded the threshold by ~1.51× now hover near 1.0 (the
#   butteraugli-equivalent regime the W44 calibration was tuned for).
#
# Follow-on candidates (NOT in Phase 8c scope):
#
# Phase 8d: bytes-tighten exit pass. For each block, try qac+1; if JOD still
#   ≤ target + ε, accept. Captures the residual outlier-cell over-allocation.
# Phase 8g (Intervention B): per-distance scale lookup (replace single
#   constant with `(d, scale)` table). Each distance band has a clear
#   monotonic trend.
# Phase 8h (Intervention BX): replace the per-block reducer entirely with
#   a cvvdp-shaped one (different reduction kernel, possibly different
#   percentile-based threshold instead of max-norm-shape predicate).
